2. Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Initialize the AptiDaily engine with the student's name and academic year.
3. Load the question bank with questions, options, correct answers, topics, difficulty levels, and explanations.
4. Filter questions matching the student's academic year.
5. Exclude questions already marked as completed.
6. If the filtered question pool is empty, use the complete question bank.
7. Shuffle the available questions randomly.
8. Select up to the specified number of questions for the daily challenge.
9. Display each question and its options.
10. Collect the selected answers.
11. Compare each selected answer with the correct answer.
12. Calculate the quiz score and update completed-question records.
13. Update topic-wise correct and total answer statistics.
14. If the quiz mode is daily, store the score against the specified date.
15. Add the quiz attempt to the history.
16. Calculate overall accuracy and display the student dashboard.
17. Stop the program.
